{%- comment -%}
  Fridge movers guide, rendered only on the fridge-movers-sydney page by titan-local-landing.
  Content: fridge types table, sizes and doorway clearance, preparation steps (HowTo schema),
  safety checklist. No prices by request: price is always given on the phone.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="tll-section tll-wrap tfg" aria-labelledby="tfg-types">
  <p class="tll-eyebrow">Every kind of fridge</p>
  <h2 id="tfg-types" class="tll-h2">What Types of Fridges Do Our Fridge Movers Handle?</h2>
  <div class="tll-rte">
    <p>From a small bar fridge to a 900 mm French-door refrigerator with an ice maker, our fridge and refrigerator removalists move them all. The bigger the fridge, the more the planning matters, so tell us the type and size when you call.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tfg-table" role="table" aria-label="Fridge types and how we move them">
    <div class="tfg-row tfg-row--head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">Fridge type</span><span role="columnheader">Typical weight</span><span role="columnheader">How we move it</span></div>
    <div class="tfg-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><strong>French-door fridge</strong></span><span role="cell">100 to 150 kg</span><span role="cell">Two movers, appliance trolley, handles off if the doorway is tight</span></div>
    <div class="tfg-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><strong>Side-by-side fridge</strong></span><span role="cell">100 to 140 kg</span><span role="cell">Doors strapped shut, water line drained and capped by you or a plumber</span></div>
    <div class="tfg-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><strong>Top or bottom-mount fridge</strong></span><span role="cell">60 to 90 kg</span><span role="cell">Upright on the trolley, wrapped in blankets</span></div>
    <div class="tfg-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><strong>Bar or wine fridge</strong></span><span role="cell">20 to 45 kg</span><span role="cell">Glass doors padded and taped, carried upright</span></div>
    <div class="tfg-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><strong>Chest freezer</strong></span><span role="cell">35 to 80 kg</span><span role="cell">Lid strapped, carried level by two movers</span></div>
    <div class="tfg-row" role="row"><span role="cell"><strong>Upright freezer</strong></span><span role="cell">50 to 90 kg</span><span role="cell">Upright on the trolley, door strapped shut</span></div>
  </div>
  <p class="tfg-note">Weights are a rough guide for common models. Check your fridge manual or the model number for the exact figure.</p>
</section>

{{ cstrip | replace: '%%T%%', 'Big French-door fridge? Tell us the model and we plan the move on the phone.' }}

<section class="tll-section tll-wrap tfg" aria-labelledby="tfg-fit">
  <p class="tll-eyebrow">Measure first</p>
  <h2 id="tfg-fit" class="tll-h2">Fridge Sizes, Weights and Doorway Clearance</h2>
  <div class="tfg-cols">
    <div class="tll-rte">
      <p>Most moving problems happen at the doorway, not in the van. Before you call, measure three things:</p>
      <p><strong>1. The fridge depth without the handles.</strong> This is the width that has to fit through your doors.<br><strong>2. The narrowest doorway or hallway</strong> on the way in, including the front door, any security door and the kitchen opening.<br><strong>3. The space where it will stand,</strong> leaving a little room at the sides and back for air to flow.</p>
      <p>A standard Sydney internal doorway is about 720 to 820 mm wide. Many French-door and side-by-side fridges are wider than that across the front, so they go through sideways on their depth, sometimes with the handles or doors removed. If it is going to be close, we tell you on the phone, not on the day.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="tfg-checks" role="list">
      <li><span>✓</span>Stairs: how many flights, and is there a turn or landing?</li>
      <li><span>✓</span>Lift: does the fridge fit, and do you need to book it?</li>
      <li><span>✓</span>Parking: can we stop close to the door at both ends?</li>
      <li><span>✓</span>Floors: timber, tiles or carpet, so we bring the right protection.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tll-section tll-wrap tfg" aria-labelledby="tfg-prep">
  <p class="tll-eyebrow">Moving day checklist</p>
  <h2 id="tfg-prep" class="tll-h2">How to Get Your Fridge Ready for Moving Day</h2>
  <ol class="tfg-steps" role="list">
    <li class="tll-glass"><b>1</b><h3>Empty the fridge</h3><p>Take out all food and drinks the day before. A full fridge is heavier and food can spill in transit.</p></li>
    <li class="tll-glass"><b>2</b><h3>Turn it off and defrost</h3><p>Switch it off the night before so the freezer can defrost. Leave the doors open and put a towel down for the water.</p></li>
    <li class="tll-glass"><b>3</b><h3>Remove loose shelves</h3><p>Take out glass shelves and drawers, or tape them in place, so nothing rattles or cracks on the way.</p></li>
    <li class="tll-glass"><b>4</b><h3>Dry it out</h3><p>Wipe the inside dry so there is no water left to leak in the van or smell when you open it.</p></li>
    <li class="tll-glass"><b>5</b><h3>Disconnect the water line</h3><p>If your fridge has an ice maker or water dispenser, have the water turned off and the line capped before we arrive.</p></li>
    <li class="tll-glass"><b>6</b><h3>Clear the way</h3><p>Move rugs, pot plants and furniture out of the path so our movers have a clear, safe route to the door.</p></li>
  </ol>
</section>

{{ cstrip | replace: '%%T%%', 'Fridge ready to go? Call and we can often move it today.' }}

<section class="tll-section tll-wrap tfg" aria-labelledby="tfg-safe">
  <p class="tll-eyebrow">Done properly, every time</p>
  <h2 id="tfg-safe" class="tll-h2">How Our Fridge Removalists Keep Your Fridge Safe</h2>
  <div class="tfg-safe">
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Always upright</h3><p>Your fridge never goes on its side. Oil in the compressor stays where it belongs, so it can be switched on again soon after delivery.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Appliance trolley</h3><p>A purpose-built trolley with straps takes the weight, so nobody is dragging or walking a heavy fridge across your floor.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Doors strapped shut</h3><p>Doors and drawers are strapped closed so they cannot swing open on stairs or in the van.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Wrapped in blankets</h3><p>Thick moving blankets protect stainless steel and glass from scratches and dents.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Floors and frames protected</h3><p>We take care around door frames, walls, lifts and floors at both ends of the move.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Two movers, every job</h3><p>One mover guides and one controls the trolley, on every step and every corner. You never need to help lift.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Strapped in the van</h3><p>The fridge is strapped upright to the wall of the van so it cannot move, tip or slide while we drive.</p></div>
    <div class="tfg-card"><h3>Covered while in our care</h3><p>Your fridge is covered from the moment we pick it up until it is standing in its new spot.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tll-section tll-wrap tfg" aria-labelledby="tfg-comm">
  <p class="tll-eyebrow">Cafés, offices and garages</p>
  <h2 id="tfg-comm" class="tll-h2">Commercial, Office and Second Fridges</h2>
  <div class="tll-rte">
    <p>We are also refrigerator movers for businesses. We move <strong>office fridges, café and shop display fridges, bar fridges and garage freezers</strong>. Tell us the model or send a photo when you call, so we can confirm it fits the van and bring the right trolley. For a fridge that is hard-wired or plumbed in, have it disconnected by a licensed tradesperson before we arrive.</p>
    <p>Moving house and only need the big items done? Our fridge movers can take your fridge, washing machine and a few heavy pieces in one trip, leaving you to move the boxes.</p>
  </div>
</section>

